{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":107455,"duration_api_ms":198688,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b7fed467-e57e-4cb9-8690-cadab9a9d926","total_cost_usd":0.5222812000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29181,"cache_read_input_tokens":82528,"output_tokens":3212,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29181,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":222,"outputTokens":10193,"cacheReadInputTokens":787752,"cacheCreationInputTokens":70683,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.21831595000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3212,"cacheReadInputTokens":82528,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29181,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30396524999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept all five amendments. Code review confirms each identifies a real issue: the snapshot mixes cached and freshly-solved values; bicarbonate_mg_per_l is provably dead chemistry input; the validator contradicts the solver's own fallback_zero_dic path; reserve_g migration double-counts mass in elemental budgets; and the detritus cap mixes raw biomass grams with organic-matter routing grams. I diverge from the planner on fr-4-8b7458ba because the code contains a genuine internal contradiction—the solver intentionally produces pH=8.5 as a stable outcome that the validator then rejects.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-daef8450","decision":"accept","rationale":"Code review confirms the snapshot reads pH from cached state.water.ph (line 87) while deriving co2_aq_mmol_per_l from a freshly solved carbonate_eq (lines 76-81). Using carbonate_eq.ph makes the snapshot self-consistent by construction—all chemistry fields come from the same equilibrium solve. The exploring agent's own conclusion states 'if you want self-consistency, you should regenerate the snapshot pH from the same fresh carbonate_eq solve,' which is exactly this amendment. No behavior change when caches are correct; eliminates a latent coupling."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-f8f0a292","decision":"accept","rationale":"Code review confirms bicarbonate_mg_per_l is definitively dead input for chemistry: it is set from the source profile (water.rs:105), immediately overwritten by resolve_carbonate_state (water.rs:110), and never referenced during water change mixing (water_change.rs uses DIC and alkalinity only). A documentation comment stating the field is display/compatibility data is accurate, low-risk, and prevents future confusion."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-8b7458ba","decision":"accept","rationale":"The code has a genuine internal contradiction. The fallback_zero_dic path (chemistry.rs:225) intentionally returns pH = CARBONATE_PH_MAX (8.5) with a 'stable' status when DIC is zero and alkalinity is positive. The validator (chemistry.rs:407) then rejects this exact value with strict inequality (eq.ph >= CARBONATE_PH_MAX). One subsystem deliberately produces a value that another subsystem deliberately rejects. Regardless of whether any shipped preset triggers this today, zero DIC with positive alkalinity is a plausible real-world configuration (remineralized water without CO2 injection). The planner's argument that this is an intentional 'interior-range contract' is undermined by the solver explicitly treating 8.5 as a valid, stable fallback. At minimum, the error should be more descriptive; better, the high bound should be inclusive to match the solver's own contract."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-3548e7f8","decision":"accept","rationale":"Code review confirms the double-counting: budget.rs counts adults_count and juveniles_count independently (lines 240-244) AND counts reserve_g independently (lines 247-248). The migration code (save.rs:366-368) reconstructs reserve_g from those same shrimp counts, injecting mass into the reserve pool that is already accounted for via the count fields. This extra N/C can immediately fund hatching/maturation via the spend path in shrimp.rs:651-656, creating shrimp that the saved state never contained."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-994ca774","decision":"accept","rationale":"Code review confirms the unit mismatch at shrimp.rs:165: periph_consumed_route_g is converted to routing grams via algae_detrital_mass_g(), but detritus_consumed is still in raw biomass grams. These are summed into daily_food_consumed_g, which per biology.rs:86-88 is documented as being on the 'shrimp-routing organic-matter basis.' The cap logic computes detritus_demand as food_demand minus periph_consumed (both raw grams), but since detritus raw grams are larger than their routing-gram equivalent, detritus-heavy diets overshoot the intended cap. The regression test (line 870) encodes the same mismatch, passing despite the bug."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7f55ff61-4cbc-41a1-8d35-6563b32c533a"}
